'\" t
.TH "ACTON\-WRAPPER" "1"
.nh
.ad l
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "NAME"
acton\-wrapper \[em] Generate Tolk, TypeScript, or Go wrappers for contracts
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBacton wrapper\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fIcontract\-name\fR
.sp
\fBacton wrapper\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fB\-\-all\fR
.sp
\fBacton wrapper \-\-catalog\fR \fIfile\fR \fB\-\-go\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Generate a wrapper for the contract identified by \fB_contract\-name_\fR from
\fBActon.toml\fR\&.
.sp
Use \fB\-\-all\fR to generate wrappers for every contract defined in \fBActon.toml\fR
without picking a single one.
.sp
Wrapper generation uses ABI emitted by the Tolk compiler from the contract source
or from a configured \fBtypes\fR interface file. In practice, the contract header is
the source of truth for typed storage accessors, incoming message helpers, and
generated get\-method bindings.
.sp
The command can also generate a Tolk stub test file, a TypeScript wrapper for
frontend integrations, or Go types, cell codecs, and getter stack codecs.
.sp
With \fB\-\-catalog FILE \-\-go\fR, the command reads an existing ABI catalog without
compiling sources. This mode does not require \fBActon.toml\fR or a source toolchain.
When a manifest is available, its project\-level Go wrapper settings are used.
.sp
For \fB\&.tolk\fR contracts, \fBacton wrapper\fR compiles the selected source directly.
For precompiled \fB\&.boc\fR contracts, it reads code from the BoC and compiles the
configured \fBtypes\fR interface file. A prior \fBacton build\fR run is not required.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.SS "Wrapper Options"
.sp
\fIcontract\-name\fR
.RS 4
Contract name from \fBActon.toml\fR to generate the wrapper for. Required unless
\fB\-\-all\fR or \fB\-\-catalog\fR is given. These three selections are mutually exclusive.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-all\fR
.RS 4
Generate wrappers for every contract defined in \fBActon.toml\fR\&.
.sp
Conflicts with \fIcontract\-name\fR, \fB\-\-catalog\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR, and \fB\-\-test\-output\fR (which
designate a single output file).
.RE
.sp
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Write the generated wrapper to an exact path.
.sp
Conflicts with \fB\-\-output\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-all\fR, and \fB\-\-go\fR\&. Go generation writes multiple
files; use \fB\-\-output\-dir\fR instead.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR \fIdir\fR
.RS 4
Write the generated wrapper to a directory and let Acton choose the file name.
For Go, write the generated package files to this directory.
.sp
Conflicts with \fB\-\-output\fR\&.
.RE
.SS "Test Stub Options"
.sp
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-test\fR
.RS 4
Generate a stub test file together with the wrapper.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-test\-output\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Write the generated test file to an exact path.
.sp
Requires \fB\-\-test\fR\&.
.sp
Conflicts with \fB\-\-all\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-test\-output\-dir\fR \fIdir\fR
.RS 4
Write the generated test file to a directory and let Acton choose the file
name.
.sp
Requires \fB\-\-test\fR\&.
.sp
Conflicts with \fB\-\-test\-output\fR\&.
.RE
.SS "TypeScript Options"
.sp
\fB\-\-ts\fR
.RS 4
Generate a TypeScript wrapper through \fB@ton/tolk\-abi\-to\-typescript@0.5.0\fR\&.
.sp
Conflicts with \fB\-\-go\fR and test stub generation.
.RE
.SS "Go Options"
.sp
\fB\-\-go\fR
.RS 4
Generate Go types, cell codecs, and getter codecs through \fBtolk\-abi\-to\-go\fR\&.
.sp
Conflicts with \fB\-\-ts\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR, \fB\-\-test\fR, \fB\-\-test\-output\fR, and \fB\-\-test\-output\-dir\fR\&.
Configured Tolk test\-stub defaults do not apply to Go generation.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-catalog\fR \fIfile\fR
.RS 4
Read a \fBschemaVersion: 1\fR ABI catalog instead of compiling project contracts.
Requires \fB\-\-go\fR\&. Conflicts with \fIcontract\-name\fR and \fB\-\-all\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-go\-package\fR \fIname\fR
.RS 4
Override the Go package name. Defaults to \fB[wrappers.go].package\fR, or \fBwrappers\fR\&.
Requires \fB\-\-go\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-go\-generator\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Use an existing generator executable instead of \fB[wrappers.go].generator\fR or
\fBtolk\-abi\-to\-go\fR on \fBPATH\fR\&. Requires \fB\-\-go\fR\&. This is an executable path, not a shell
command with arguments. Relative CLI paths are resolved from the current directory.
.RE
.SS "Display Options"
.sp
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIwhen\fR
.RS 4
Control when to use colored output.
.sp
Possible values: \fBauto\fR, \fBalways\fR, \fBnever\fR
.RE
.SS "Project Options"
.sp
\fB\-\-manifest\-path\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Path to the \fBActon.toml\fR file to use for this invocation.
.sp
Use this when running the command outside the project directory or when the
manifest lives at a non\-default location.
.RE
.sp
\fB\-\-project\-root\fR \fIpath\fR
.RS 4
Path to the project root to use for configuration discovery and relative
defaults.
.sp
This conflicts with \fB\-\-manifest\-path\fR\&.
.RE
.SH "ABI REQUIREMENTS"
Wrapper generation depends on the contract ABI exposed by the Tolk compiler.
The following helpers describe Tolk and TypeScript wrappers; Go generates codecs
rather than deployment or RPC clients.
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBstorage: ...\fR enables typed storage helpers such as \fBfromStorage\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fBincomingMessages: ...\fR enables \fBsend{Message}\fR helpers
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'declared get methods are emitted as wrapper methods
.RE
.sp
If \fBincomingMessages\fR is missing, message\-sending helpers are not generated. If
\fBstorage\fR is missing, storage helpers fall back to an untyped initializer.
.SH "TYPESCRIPT GENERATION"
\fBacton wrapper \-\-ts\fR shells out to \fBnpx @ton/tolk\-abi\-to\-typescript@0.5.0\fR\&.
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'Node.js, npm, and \fBnpx\fR must be available in \fBPATH\fR
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'existing wrapper files at the target path are overwritten
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB\-\-ts\fR cannot be combined with \fB\-\-test\fR, \fB\-\-test\-output\fR, or
\fB\-\-test\-output\-dir\fR
.RE
.SH "CONFIGURATION"
Project\-wide defaults can be configured in \fBActon.toml\fR:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
[wrappers.tolk]
output\-dir = "wrappers"
generate\-test = true
test\-output\-dir = "tests"

[wrappers.typescript]
output\-dir = "wrappers\-ts"
[wrappers.go]
output\-dir = "wrappers\-go"
package = "wrappers"
generator = "tolk\-abi\-to\-go"
.fi
.RE
.sp
Each contract can override the same settings without changing the defaults for
other contracts:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
[contracts.Counter.wrappers.tolk]
output\-dir = "generated/counter"
generate\-test = false
test\-output\-dir = "tests/generated/counter"
[contracts.Counter.wrappers.typescript]
output\-dir = "app/src/wrappers/counter"
.fi
.RE
.sp
Settings are resolved field by field. CLI flags have the highest priority,
then \fB[contracts.<name>.wrappers.*]\fR, then \fB[wrappers.*]\fR, and finally the
wrapper command defaults. An omitted per\-contract field inherits the
project\-wide value. An explicit per\-contract \fBgenerate\-test = false\fR overrides
a project\-wide \fBtrue\fR\&. With \fB\-\-all\fR, Acton resolves these settings separately
for every contract for Tolk and TypeScript. Go \fB\-\-all\fR produces one package and
uses only project\-level settings and CLI overrides, not per\-contract settings.
Single\-contract Go runs also honor \fB[contracts.<name>.wrappers.go]\fR overrides.
.sp
Configured Go output directories and generator paths such as \fB\&./bin/tolk\-abi\-to\-go\fR
are project\-root\-relative; bare generator names are searched on \fBPATH\fR\&. CLI
\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR, \fB\-\-catalog\fR, and \fB\-\-go\-generator\fR paths are cwd\-relative.
.sp
For a precompiled \fB\&.boc\fR contract, configure \fBtypes\fR next to \fBsrc\fR so wrapper
generation can read ABI from the Tolk interface file:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
[contracts.Precompiled]
src = "contracts/Precompiled.boc"
types = "contracts/Precompiled.types.tolk"
.fi
.RE
.sp
Do not put dependencies on the BoC contract itself: it is already compiled.
Instead, put \fBdepends = ["Precompiled"]\fR on the \fB\&.tolk\fR contract that needs the
BoC code.
.SH "GO GENERATION"
Install or build the generator separately. Acton runs the executable directly;
it never downloads a runtime or falls back to npm. For published code, install a
pinned revision containing the generator:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
go install github.com/toncenter/ton\-indexer/ton\-index\-go/index/acton/cmd/tolk\-abi\-to\-go@<version>
.fi
.RE
.sp
Replace \fB<version>\fR with a published commit revision. Do not assume an Acton
release tag exists for this Go module. For an unpublished checkout, build locally
and select the binary with \fB\-\-go\-generator /path/to/tolk\-abi\-to\-go\fR instead.
.sp
Generated files import \fBgithub.com/toncenter/ton\-indexer/ton\-index\-go/index/acton\fR\&.
The Go runtime does not require CGO. Add that module at a compatible pinned
revision to the consuming Go project. Acton does not modify \fBgo.mod\fR\&.
.sp
Project generation passes one temporary catalog containing the selected contract
IDs, code hashes, and compiler ABIs to the generator. \fB\-\-all\fR compiles every
eligible ABI before invoking it once, so one contract cannot overwrite another\[cq]s
registry. Precompiled BoCs without \fBtypes\fR are skipped by \fB\-\-all\fR; an explicitly
selected BoC requires \fBtypes\fR\&. An empty eligible selection is an error.
.sp
Treat the output directory as one generated package. To combine contracts, use
\fB\-\-all\fR or a catalog rather than repeated single\-contract runs into the same
directory. The generator owns filenames and replacement of generated artifacts.
Its stdout, stderr (including unsupported\-codec diagnostics), and failures are
propagated. Unsupported ABI roots may remain metadata\-only; inspect diagnostics.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB0\fR: Wrapper generation completed successfully.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\fB1\fR: The contract could not be found or compiled, ABI data was missing, the
external generator could not run, or an output file could not be written.
.RE
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 1.\h'+01'Generate the default Tolk wrapper:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton wrapper Counter
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 2.\h'+01'Generate a wrapper and stub test:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton wrapper Counter \-\-test
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 3.\h'+01'Generate a TypeScript wrapper:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton wrapper Counter \-\-ts
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 4.\h'+01'Generate into custom locations:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton wrapper Counter \-\-output\-dir tests/generated
acton wrapper Counter \-\-test \-\-test\-output\-dir tests/generated
acton wrapper Counter \-\-ts \-\-output\-dir wrappers\-ts
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 5.\h'+01'Generate a frontend\-oriented TypeScript wrapper layout:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton wrapper Counter \-\-ts \-\-output\-dir app/src/wrappers\-ts
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 6.\h'+01'Generate wrappers for every contract in \fBActon.toml\fR:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton wrapper \-\-all
acton wrapper \-\-all \-\-ts
acton wrapper \-\-all \-\-output\-dir wrappers/generated
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 7.\h'+01'Generate Go codecs for one contract or the entire project:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton wrapper Counter \-\-go
acton wrapper \-\-all \-\-go \-\-output\-dir internal/contracts \-\-go\-package contracts
.fi
.RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
\h'-04' 8.\h'+01'Generate Go codecs from a catalog without an Acton project:
.sp
.RS 4
.nf
acton wrapper \-\-catalog data\-abis.json \-\-go \-\-output\-dir generated \-\-go\-package catalog
acton wrapper \-\-catalog data\-abis.json \-\-go \-\-go\-generator ./bin/tolk\-abi\-to\-go
.fi
.RE
.RE
